From b1f125215458e6e1c2e11097ca3c2a080aab3fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:43:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fork: read assistant turns aloud with the daemon's TTS

Adds a speaker button next to Copy in each completed assistant turn. It
sends the turn's text (the same text Copy uses) to the daemon, which strips
markdown (code blocks become "Code block.", links keep their label, tags
are removed) and plays it through the existing TTSManager path used by the
voice `speak` tool. The button turns into Stop while that turn plays and is
disabled while any other speech is playing.

Protocol: speech_replay_request / speech_replay_cancel inbound,
speech_replay_finished outbound, gated by server_info features.speechReplay.
The button is also hidden unless voice readiness reports TTS available.

In voice mode the audio is flagged isVoiceMode so the app plays it through
the voice runtime, which shares the capture engine's echo cancellation and
barge-in: speaking over a replay cancels it like it cancels live speech.
Cancel never interrupts the agent; a voice `speak` call supersedes a replay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
